WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.701
[music playing]

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:07.540
- Ingrid Visser and Kina
Scollay are looking for evidence

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.677
that Orca are hunting
great white sharks

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.812
in New Zealand waters.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.616
Ingrid has evidence that
there's a disturbing pattern

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.618
in Orca hunting.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:23.490
New Zealand Orca are hunting
Sevengill sharks, just

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.692
like the South African Orca.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:32.565
Sevengill sharks grow to nine
feet long and 200 pounds,

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:37.237
a much larger meal for
an Orca than a small ray.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:41.674
But the Sevengill
shark is no easy prey.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.011
- Sevengills are relatively
new on the Orca menu.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.714
But I've seen it
a few times now.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.849
You see the Orca,
and they're very,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.185
very precise in how they do it.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.287
And I've got footage of
Orca with the Sevengills,

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:55.722
where they've ripped
the pectoral fin

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.824
right under the
pectoral girdle there,

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:01.227
and they've extracted the liver.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.096
[voices exclaiming]

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.397
- Shark!

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.665
Shark!

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.534
- One of the things
I find fascinating

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.170
is how the Sevengills will
actually turn and defend

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.805
themselves against the Orca.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.845
The way the Orca
hunt the Sevengills

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.447
is pretty impressive.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.215
First of all, they'll
come in and they'll

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.483
karate chop the shark.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.084
So they'll just come
and lift their tail

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.653
up and whack them on the back.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.129
Then they grab the sharks by the
pectoral fin and rip them open

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.932
and pull the livers out.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:43.102
- Ingrid captured rare footage
of Orcas hunting Sevengills

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.437
in northern New Zealand.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:08.495
Their precision in hunting
for shark liver is clear.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.435
[music playing]

